  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.1. Increased capacity of Member States to create an enabling environment for entrepreneurship and sustainable enterprises</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022-23, the Jordan Cooperative Corporation (JCC),  a public entity in charge of overseeing cooperatives in Jordan, operationalized the National Cooperative Strategy for Jordan for 2021-2025 via the establishment of an action plan with outcomes prioritizing national and international investment in the development of the cooperative movement. The strategy is a product of consultations between line ministries, cooperatives, civil society and workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; organizations. It reflects a conducive environment for cooperative development, efficient service infrastructure and self-reliant cooperatives. With the support from the Kingdom of the Netherlands, the ILO supported the Jordan Cooperatives Corporation in the administration of a review of the cooperative legislation and its capacity development. 

In July 2022, the ILO supported the Jordan Cooperatives Corporation in launching &#x201c;Practical Occupational Safety and Health Training for Cooperatives in Agriculture&#x201d; targeting key  institutions including government, international and local organizations, the Jordan Cooperatives Corporation, and workers and employers.

In January 2023, the ILO supported the Jordan Cooperatives Corporation in organizing a workshop to review proposed amendments to the law, to align it with the international standards including the Promotion of Cooperatives Recommendation No. 193. The workshop included representatives from social partners and cooperatives themselves, and provided feedback on the proposed amendments for further revision.</narrative>
   </description>
