  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises and their support systems to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022-23, the Jordanian Government and social partners supported the Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises,  women entrepreneurship and  women-led enterprises via the establishment of a national financial inclusion strategy, and tools and instruments that are adapted for the different target groups. Support included developing adequate digital finance, micro-finance and Small and Medium Enterprises financial products for women, youth and refugees. 

The Jordan Chamber of Industry enhanced services provided to Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises through an agrifood sector pilot, whereby it oversaw the review of productivity bottlenecks within 20 Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises and designed targeted support to address them. The Jordan Chamber of Industry staff were trained on the assessment methodology and subsequently they developed action plans for the Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises to improve productivity and working conditions. With the support from the Kingdom of the Netherlands, in December 2022, the ILO supported Jordan Chamber of Industry in the organisation of a training of trainers on Sustaining Competitive and Responsible Enterprises (SCORE) whereby Jordan Chamber of Industry staff delivered direct support to the agrifood&#x2019;s Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises to overcome productivity bottlenecks.

In 2022-23, the ILO supported Jordan Cooperatives Corporation to launch a training of trainers on the elimination of child labour for various institutions spanning governmental, international and local organizations, and worker&#x2019;s and employer&#x2019;s groups.</narrative>
   </description>
